1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,920
Aarav lives on a long, straight road.

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:06,937
Ride three kilometres east, and
he is three kilometres from home.

3
00:00:07,337 --> 00:00:11,782
Ride three kilometres west, and he
is still three kilometres from home.

4
00:00:11,782 --> 00:00:12,965
Not minus three.

5
00:00:13,415 --> 00:00:16,091
Aarav noticed this on his ride to college.

6
00:00:16,441 --> 00:00:18,227
Direction can be negative.

7
00:00:18,227 --> 00:00:19,555
Distance never is.

8
00:00:19,555 --> 00:00:21,899
Which function knows the difference?

9
00:00:22,399 --> 00:00:23,769
The modulus function.

10
00:00:23,769 --> 00:00:28,062
And with it today, the rational
function, which has a gap you can never

11
00:00:28,062 --> 00:00:28,962
cross.

12
00:00:29,276 --> 00:00:31,716
Put home at zero on a number line.

13
00:00:31,716 --> 00:00:34,185
East is positive, west is negative.

14
00:00:34,185 --> 00:00:35,680
Call his position x.

15
00:00:36,081 --> 00:00:40,333
His distance from home is written
as x between two straight bars.

16
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:41,955
We read it as mod x.

17
00:00:42,355 --> 00:00:44,244
The rule has two parts.

18
00:00:44,244 --> 00:00:47,478
If x is zero or more, mod x is just x.

19
00:00:47,478 --> 00:00:50,413
If x is negative, mod x is minus x.

20
00:00:51,163 --> 00:00:53,077
Minus x for a negative x?

21
00:00:53,077 --> 00:00:53,977
Yes.

22
00:00:53,602 --> 00:00:57,688
If x is minus three, then
minus x is minus, minus three.

23
00:00:57,688 --> 00:00:59,170
That is plus three.

24
00:00:59,170 --> 00:01:01,290
The minus sign flips it back.

25
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:04,183
So mod x is never negative.

26
00:01:04,183 --> 00:01:08,971
Its domain is R, and its range is
zero and every positive number.

27
00:01:09,621 --> 00:01:14,589
Now watch the graph draw, as Aarav
rides from four kilometres west to four

28
00:01:14,589 --> 00:01:15,829
kilometres east.

29
00:01:16,228 --> 00:01:19,767
On the west side, his distance
falls as he gets closer.

30
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:21,555
At home, it touches zero.

31
00:01:21,555 --> 00:01:23,832
On the east side, it rises again.

32
00:01:24,232 --> 00:01:28,006
The result is a V, with
its corner at the origin.

33
00:01:28,006 --> 00:01:30,602
The left arm is y equals minus x.

34
00:01:30,602 --> 00:01:32,860
The right arm is y equals x.

35
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:36,617
Now measure from a friend's
house at k instead.

36
00:01:36,617 --> 00:01:39,011
The distance is mod of x minus k.

37
00:01:39,011 --> 00:01:42,279
Watch k slide, and the
whole V slides with it.

38
00:01:42,929 --> 00:01:44,089
Side by side.

39
00:01:44,089 --> 00:01:47,290
The identity, y equals x, keeps the sign.

40
00:01:47,290 --> 00:01:49,492
Minus three stays minus three.

41
00:01:49,892 --> 00:01:53,321
The modulus, y equals
mod x, removes the sign.

42
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:55,187
Minus three becomes three.

43
00:01:55,187 --> 00:01:57,751
For positive inputs, the two agree.

44
00:01:58,351 --> 00:01:59,534
Now you try.

45
00:01:59,534 --> 00:02:03,104
Is mod x equal to x for
every real number x?

46
00:02:03,104 --> 00:02:04,574
Pause and decide.

47
00:02:07,774 --> 00:02:08,674
No!

48
00:02:08,281 --> 00:02:10,560
Only when x is zero or more.

49
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:14,844
If x is minus two, mod x
is two, but x is minus two.

50
00:02:15,494 --> 00:02:16,599
Remember this.

51
00:02:16,599 --> 00:02:20,047
Modulus keeps the size,
and throws away the sign.

52
00:02:20,747 --> 00:02:22,733
Now, rational functions.

53
00:02:22,733 --> 00:02:27,946
A rational function is one polynomial
divided by another, f of x over g

54
00:02:27,946 --> 00:02:30,748
of x, where g of x is not zero.

55
00:02:31,148 --> 00:02:33,324
The simplest is one over x.

56
00:02:33,324 --> 00:02:38,353
Its domain is every real number except
zero, because we can never divide

57
00:02:38,353 --> 00:02:39,253
by zero.

58
00:02:39,608 --> 00:02:42,564
Watch x come closer to
zero from the right.

59
00:02:42,564 --> 00:02:44,122
One over one is one.

60
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:45,942
One over a tenth is ten.

61
00:02:45,942 --> 00:02:48,325
One over a hundredth is a hundred.

62
00:02:48,725 --> 00:02:52,121
The curve shoots upward, but
it never touches the y axis.

63
00:02:52,121 --> 00:02:54,927
Come in from the left,
and it shoots downward.

64
00:02:55,327 --> 00:02:58,189
And when x is huge, one over x is tiny.

65
00:02:58,189 --> 00:03:01,496
The curve hugs the x axis,
but never reaches it.

66
00:03:02,146 --> 00:03:03,078
Quick one.

67
00:03:03,078 --> 00:03:05,800
Is zero in the range of one over x?

68
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,118
Pause and think.

69
00:03:10,318 --> 00:03:11,218
No!

70
00:03:10,836 --> 00:03:13,904
One divided by any number is never zero.

71
00:03:13,904 --> 00:03:17,513
So the range of one
over x is R, minus zero.

72
00:03:18,163 --> 00:03:19,898
Now, one worked example.

73
00:03:20,248 --> 00:03:23,040
Solve mod of x minus two equals five.

74
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:24,440
Step one.

75
00:03:24,396 --> 00:03:27,967
Mod of x minus two is the
distance of x from two.

76
00:03:27,967 --> 00:03:30,662
So we want points five away from two.

77
00:03:31,412 --> 00:03:32,341
Step two.

78
00:03:32,341 --> 00:03:36,798
If x minus two is zero or
more, x minus two equals five.

79
00:03:36,798 --> 00:03:38,147
So x is seven.

80
00:03:38,897 --> 00:03:39,944
Step three.

81
00:03:39,944 --> 00:03:44,700
If x minus two is negative,
minus of x minus two equals five.

82
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:46,464
So x is minus three.

83
00:03:47,214 --> 00:03:48,114
Step four.

84
00:03:48,093 --> 00:03:48,993
Check.

85
00:03:48,709 --> 00:03:50,477
Seven minus two is five.

86
00:03:50,477 --> 00:03:54,438
Minus three minus two is minus
five, and its mod is five.

87
00:03:55,188 --> 00:03:57,534
Two answers: seven and minus three.

88
00:03:57,534 --> 00:04:01,092
One on each side of two,
like the two arms of the V.

89
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:03,208
Now, the exam trap.

90
00:04:03,558 --> 00:04:05,824
What is the square root of x squared?

91
00:04:05,824 --> 00:04:09,260
Many students cancel the root
and the square, and write x.

92
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:11,663
But try x equals minus four.

93
00:04:11,663 --> 00:04:16,288
x squared is sixteen, and the square
root of sixteen is four, not minus

94
00:04:16,288 --> 00:04:17,188
four.

95
00:04:16,846 --> 00:04:19,527
The square root of x squared is mod x.

96
00:04:20,177 --> 00:04:21,690
Where is this asked?

97
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:26,229
In JEE Main, as equations with
mod, where you count the solutions.

98
00:04:26,229 --> 00:04:31,357
And in PUC board papers, as find the
domain and range of a modulus function.

99
00:04:31,957 --> 00:04:33,262
Exam level now.

100
00:04:33,262 --> 00:04:36,722
How many real solutions
does this equation have?

101
00:04:36,722 --> 00:04:38,082
Pause and solve.

102
00:04:43,482 --> 00:04:44,948
The answer is D.

103
00:04:44,948 --> 00:04:46,277
Infinitely many.

104
00:04:46,777 --> 00:04:48,433
Read it as distances.

105
00:04:48,433 --> 00:04:51,488
Mod x minus one is the distance from one.

106
00:04:51,488 --> 00:04:54,758
Mod x minus three is
the distance from three.

107
00:04:55,258 --> 00:04:58,397
The two points, one and
three, are exactly two apart.

108
00:04:58,897 --> 00:05:03,773
For any x between one and three, the
two distances add up to exactly two.

109
00:05:04,273 --> 00:05:07,412
Outside that stretch,
the sum is more than two.

110
00:05:07,412 --> 00:05:09,814
So every x from one to three works.

111
00:05:09,814 --> 00:05:11,489
Infinitely many solutions.

112
00:05:12,089 --> 00:05:13,553
Here is your recap.

113
00:05:13,553 --> 00:05:15,058
Screenshot this card.

114
00:05:18,258 --> 00:05:21,095
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

115
00:05:21,495 --> 00:05:22,395
One.

116
00:05:22,011 --> 00:05:23,997
What is mod of minus seven?

117
00:05:24,897 --> 00:05:25,797
Two.

118
00:05:25,432 --> 00:05:28,629
What is the domain of
one over x minus four?

119
00:05:29,529 --> 00:05:30,429
Three.

120
00:05:30,203 --> 00:05:33,050
Solve mod of x plus one equals three.

121
00:05:34,150 --> 00:05:37,368
Next time: age is counted
in completed years.

122
00:05:37,368 --> 00:05:40,533
Sixteen point nine years
old is still sixteen.

123
00:05:40,533 --> 00:05:43,687
Meet the signum and
greatest integer functions.
